    "description": "PARKED — additive to the baseline custom file properties; we would apply both.\n\nWhy it exists: custom file properties are readable via the API but are NOT VISIBLE OR FILTERABLE IN THE DRIVE WEB INTERFACE. Drive Labels are the upgrade that lets analysts and auditors filter and search proofs inside Drive itself. A genuine usability gain for anyone reviewing proofs in bulk.\n\nDepends entirely on the WagerTech side:\n\n* Google Workspace Business Standard or above — Labels are NOT available on lower editions\n\n* A Workspace admin to define the label taxonomy in the Google Admin console. LABELS CANNOT BE CREATED BY AN INTEGRATION; they are admin-configured structure. Needs a short session with their admin to set fields matching our metadata table\n\n* Ceiling of roughly ten labels per file, which our set fits comfortably\n\nNot needed for the POC and NOT needed for automation — automation reads the custom properties. Worth it only if humans will browse and filter the library in Drive.\n\nEffort: \\~3h on our side plus the admin session.\n\nSource: Drive Storage doc §3.2, D5.",
